{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8f879536012842e8ddc896470e33cfa63fca6e6aa9baaef0d4065f2f38e176c7","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar CLI comment command","key_entities":["rebar comment","--body-file","--body","create","edit","session-log","tag","untag","archive","set-verify-commands","args[:min_args]","Gerrit 1197","ac24eacab"],"problem_keywords":["silent data loss","cli argument parsing","positional argument","flag confusion","exit code 0","durability"],"propositions":["rebar comment silently accepts flag-like tokens (--body-file, --body) as the comment body instead of rejecting them, destroying the intended content while exiting 0","a positional-body argument beginning with - is not rejected; the flag is stored as body text and any surplus positional argument containing the actual content is discarded by args slicing","the escape hatch -- must allow writing bodies that legitimately begin with -, e.g. rebar comment <id> -- \"-starts with dash\"","the same footgun and guard pattern must be applied across all positional-body commands: comment, tag, untag, archive, set-verify-commands, create, edit, session-log"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787543516472364001,"uuid":"5b51232b-42f4-4024-ba5f-9e3096e32261"}